Package: RFindsc
Title: Direction-Aware Panel Scoring for Single-Cell RNA-Seq
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tomoyuki", "Murano", , "tomoyuki.murano@fujita-hu.ac.jp", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Miyakawa", "Lab", role = "fnd")
  )
Description: RFind-sc scores each cell against case-vs-control gene panels with
    the Running Fisher test: two ranked gene lists are compared by the smallest
    hypergeometric p-value over every pair of cut-offs (an unordered gene
    set is used whole), and the four up/down pairs are combined into one
    signed score. Per-cell UP/DOWN signatures are ranked by the P2 Pearson
    residual of observed versus baseline-expected counts,
    (obs - exp)/sqrt(exp + 1). Panels consist of
    paired UP and DOWN gene lists (or a single gene group), producing signed
    per-cell scores (case-like positive, control-like negative). The package
    ships the reference axes of the RFind-sc paper (Hammond: DAM, Maturity,
    Interferon, G2M; De Donno: Glucocorticoid, Seizure, UPR, NF-kB), with
    helpers to pull MSigDB collections and auto-pair C2 CGP '_UP/_DN' panels.
